{"diagnosis": "Trace shows loopback send 0xa5 with TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received, so recv_buf_valid never asserted (stayed 0 vs expected 1). Root cause in excerpt line 92 assigns recv_buf_valid <= 2 in state 10, which truncates to 0 for a 1-bit valid flag so the received byte is never signaled. CONE_SLICE provides no simpleuart coverage (0/1 resolved, only spiflash/system refs), so trace + excerpt lines 89-93 win.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
 				10: begin
 					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
- 						recv_buf_valid <= 2;
+ 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart byte 0xa5 received, no timeout trap"}

